\title{Vector reductions}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-15}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{language}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{pr}{1001}
\import{base-macros}

\p{\code{\verb~|core::simd~} gains \code{\verb~|reduce_add~}, \code{\verb~|reduce_mul~}, \code{\verb~|reduce_min~}, \code{\verb~|reduce_max~}, \code{\verb~|reduce_and~}, \code{\verb~|reduce_or~} and \code{\verb~|reduce_xor~}, which combine the lanes of a vector into one value; a vector of several dimensions is flattened first. The floating-point sum and product combine in lane order, and \code{\verb~|reduce_add_reassoc~} and \code{\verb~|reduce_mul_reassoc~} allow any order. Each has a masked form such as \code{\verb~|reduce_add_masked(v, m)~}, in which a masked lane contributes the identity of the combination, see [dec-5088](dec-5088). \pr{1001}.}
